name: mysqld_multi
description: |-
  mysqld_multi version 3.0 by Jani Tolonen

  Description: mysqld_multi can be used to start, reload, or stop any number of separate mysqld processes running in different TCP/IP ports and UNIX sockets.

  mysqld_multi can read group [mysqld_multi] from my.cnf file. You may want to put options mysqld=... and mysqladmin=... there. Since version 2.10 these options can also be given under groups [mysqld#], which gives more control over different versions. One can have the default mysqld and mysqladmin under group [mysqld_multi], but this is not mandatory. Please note that if mysqld or mysqladmin is missing from both [mysqld_multi] and [mysqld#], a group that is tried to be used, mysqld_multi will abort with an error.

  mysqld_multi will search for groups named [mysqld#] from my.cnf (or the given --defaults-extra-file=...), where '#' can be any positive integer starting from 1. These groups should be the same as the regular [mysqld] group, but with those port, socket and any other options that are to be used with each separate mysqld process. The number in the group name has another function; it can be used for starting, reloading, stopping, or reporting any specific mysqld server.
usage:
- 'Usage: mysqld_multi [OPTIONS] {start|reload|stop|report} [GNR,GNR,GNR...]'
flags:
- long: no-defaults
  description: Do not read any defaults file
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: defaults-file
  value_name: '...'
  value_kind: Required
  description: Read only this configuration file, do not read the standard system-wide and user-specific files
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: defaults-extra-file
  value_name: '...'
  value_kind: Required
  description: Read this configuration file in addition to the standard system-wide and user-specific files
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: example
  description: Give an example of a config file with extra information.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: help
  description: Print this help and exit.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: log
  value_name: '...'
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'Log file. Full path to and the name for the log file. NOTE: If the file exists, everything will be appended. Using:'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: mysqladmin
  value_name: '...'
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'mysqladmin binary to be used for a server shutdown. Since version 2.10 this can be given within groups [mysqld#] Using:'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: mysqld
  value_name: '...'
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'mariadbd binary to be used. Note that you can give mariadbd-safe to this option also. The options are passed to mysqld. Just make sure you have mariadbd in your PATH or fix mariadbd-safe. Using: Please note: Since mysqld_multi version 2.3 you can also give this option inside groups [mysqld#] in ~/.my.cnf, where ''#'' stands for an integer (number) of the group in question. This will be recognised as a special option and will not be passed to the mysqld. This will allow one to start different mysqld versions with mysqld_multi.'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: no-log
  description: Print to stdout instead of the log file. By default the log file is turned on.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: password
  value_name: '...'
  value_kind: Required
  description: Password for mysqladmin user.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: silent
  description: Disable warnings.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: tcp-ip
  description: Connect to the MariaDB server(s) via the TCP/IP port instead of the UNIX socket. This affects stopping and reporting. If a socket file is missing, the server may still be running, but can be accessed only via the TCP/IP port. By default connecting is done via the UNIX socket.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: user
  value_name: '...'
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'mysqladmin user. Using: root'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: verbose
  description: Be more verbose.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: version
  description: Print the version number and exit.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- long: wsrep-new-cluster
  description: Bootstrap a cluster.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
provenance:
  sources:
  - help-text
  confidence: 0.5
children_filled: true
